    I understand the submission requirements, the functions I can override, and the training process, including the Ray Distributed Training and automatic debugging. I''ve also noted the limitations of the baseline (Evaluation ID 1), which treats neurons as independent.


    To proceed effectively, my next step is to understand the underlying training framework by reading `defaults.py`, as explicitly recommended in the task description. This will give me a clearer picture of how my `submission.py` functions will integrate with the system.


