parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 307\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher committed to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 28,750 / 600,000 used (5%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aethel I Global Context Shared-Neuron MLP' (ID: 549) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029911029910911022\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0198\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0239\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0312\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0337\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 549\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code through two iterations. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two distinct bugs:\n\n### Bug 1: Dataclass\
    \ Field Ordering (submission_v1)\n**Error:** `TypeError: non-default argument 'dropout_rate' follows default argument`\n\nIn the `GlobalContextSharedNeuronMLP` class, the field definition had:\n```python\nclass GlobalContextSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32  # Has default value\n    dropout_rate: float        # No default value - ERROR!\n```\n\nPython dataclasses (which Flax modules use) require all fields with default values to come AFTER fields without defaults.\n\n### Bug 2: Incorrect Preprocessing Logic (submission_v2)\n**Error:** `ValueError: axis 3 is out of bounds for array of dimension 3`\n\nThe `GlobalContextMLPWrapper.init()` and `apply()` methods were manually replicating the preprocessing logic that should only exist in the model's `__call__` method. This caused two problems:\n\n1. **Wrong concatenation operation:** Used `jnp.concatenate([x, global_avg_input_repeated], axis=-1)` which creates shape `(batch_size, input_horizon,\
    \ num_neurons*2)` instead of the intended `(batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons, 2)`.\n\n2. **Redundant preprocessing:** The wrapper was preprocessing the data before passing it to the model, but the model's `__call__` method also performs preprocessing. This double-preprocessing broke the expected data flow.\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### Fix for submission_v2:\nReordered the dataclass fields to put non-default fields first:\n```python\nclass GlobalContextSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int           # No default\n    dropout_rate: float        # No default\n    output_horizon: int = 32   # Has default - must come last\n```\n\n### Fix for submission_v3 (FINAL):\n1. **Removed redundant preprocessing** from `init()` and `apply()` methods\n2. **Fixed the concatenation logic** in the model by using `jnp.stack()` instead of `jnp.concatenate()`:\n```python\n# OLD (incorrect):\nx_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, global_avg_input_repeated], axis=-1)\n\n# NEW (correct):\nx_augmented\
    \ = jnp.stack([x, global_avg_input_repeated], axis=-1)\n```\n\nThe `stack()` operation properly creates a new dimension for the two features (original neuron activity and global average), resulting in the correct shape `(batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons, 2)`.\n\n3. **Simplified wrapper methods** to just pass raw input directly to the model:\n```python\ndef init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    # No preprocessing - let the model handle it\n    variables = self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n                                dummy_input, training=True)\n    return variables\n```\n\n## Result\nThe submission now runs successfully without crashing. The code executes for the full timeout period (300+ seconds), indicating that the training loop is functioning correctly with proper data flow through the neural network.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update\
    \ them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the enhanced shared MLP.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 64,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1\n    }\n\nclass GlobalContextSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Shared-neuron MLP enhanced with global mean context.\n    Each neuron's 4-timestep input is augmented with the global mean activity\n    (across all neurons) for those same 4 timesteps.\n    \"\"\"\n    hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n        # 1. Calculate global average over neurons for the input timesteps\n        # x shape: (batch_size, input_horizon,\
    \ num_neurons)\n        # global_avg_input shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, 1)\n        global_avg_input = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n        # Repeat for all neurons\n        # global_avg_input_repeated shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n        global_avg_input_repeated = jnp.tile(global_avg_input, (1, 1, num_neurons))\n\n        # 2. Stack original neuron input with global context along a new dimension\n        # x shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n        # global_avg_input_repeated shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n        # Stack along new axis: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons, 2)\n        x_augmented = jnp.stack([x, global_avg_input_repeated], axis=-1)\n\n        # Transpose to (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon, 2)\n        x_augmented = jnp.transpose(x_augmented, (0, 2, 1, 3))\n        # Reshape to (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon * 2) = (B*N, 8)\n        x_reshaped = jnp.reshape(x_augmented, (batch_size\
    \ * num_neurons, input_horizon * 2))\n\n        # Shared MLP: input_dim (input_horizon * 2 = 8) -> hidden (64) -> output (32)\n        # Layer 1 with BatchNorm and Dropout\n        x_processed = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_reshaped)\n        x_processed = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x_processed)\n        x_processed = nn.relu(x_processed)\n        x_processed = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x_processed)\n\n        # Output layer\n        x_processed = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x_processed)\n\n        # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n        # From (batch_size * num_neurons, output_horizon)\n        x_output = jnp.reshape(x_processed, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n        x_output = jnp.transpose(x_output, (0, 2, 1)) # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n        return x_output\n\nclass GlobalContextMLPWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n\
    \    Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = GlobalContextSharedNeuronMLP(\n            hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        # dummy_input will be (batch_size, 4, 71721)\n        # Just pass it directly to the model - the model handles the preprocessing\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # Just pass x directly to the model - the model handles the preprocessing\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n\
    \                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the global-context enhanced shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n    return GlobalContextMLPWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute\
    \ loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 614911 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 614914\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_size': 64, 'dropout_rate': 0.1}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.080329   |   0.032103  \n   2    |   0.031672   |   0.030555  \n   3    |   0.030487   |   0.030336  \n   4    |   0.030223   |   0.030220  \n   5    |   0.030224   |   0.030270  \n   6    |   0.030141   |   0.030318  \n   7    |   0.030141   |   0.030189  \n   8    |   0.030098   |   0.030305  \n   9    |   0.030053   |   0.030654  \n  10    |   0.030008   |   0.030257  \n  11    |   0.030006   |   0.030014  \n  12    |   0.029978   |   0.030093\
