tick: 318
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. I have completed my reflection session and am now ready to execute the \"Experiment\" phase of the Stagnation Protocol. My first idea to test is the \"Deeper Shared MLP,\" aiming to increase model capacity within the existing shared-neuron framework.\n\nI will implement a `DeeperSharedNeuronMLP` model with two hidden layers, starting with `hidden_size=64` for each, consistent with the single hidden layer in the baseline. This will allow me to assess if simply adding more non-linearity improves performance on the ZAPBench task.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers)\"\ntags: \"mlp, shared-weights, deeper-network, baseline-enhancement, neural-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This submission explores increasing the capacity of the Shared-Neuron MLP baseline by adding an additional hidden layer. The model now features two hidden layers (64 neurons each) with BatchNorm and Dropout, aiming\
    \ to capture more complex non-linear temporal relationships within each neuron's 4-timestep input. All other hyperparameters and the shared-weight paradigm remain consistent with the baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the deeper shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [64, 64], # Two hidden layers, each with 64 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Deeper shared-neuron MLP with multiple hidden layers, BatchNorm and Dropout.\n      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n          # From (batch_size, 4, num_neurons) to (batch_size * num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply multiple hidden layers\n          for i, hidden_size in enumerate(self.hidden_sizes):\n              x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n              x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2,\
    \ 1))  # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with BatchNorm stats.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"\
    Apply network with proper handling of BatchNorm and Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the deeper shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Let''s Deepen the MLP!**


  Okay, I''m going to take the first idea from my reflection and run with it: a Deeper Shared MLP. This seems like a promising direction. Here''s my plan:


  First, I need to define the hyperparameters.  I''ll use `learning_rate` and `dropout_rate` similar to the baseline, but the key is a `hidden_sizes` list. I''m thinking something like `[64, 64]` for a two-layer structure to start.


  Next, I''ll create a new Flax module called `DeeperSharedNeuronMLP`. Inside, the `__call__` method will be where the magic happens. I''ll iterate through the `hidden_sizes` list and construct a series of `nn.Dense` layers, each followed by `nn.BatchNorm`, `nn.relu`, and `nn.Dropout`.  This should give us the deeper architecture we''re after.


  It''s crucial that I keep the input and output reshaping consistent with the baseline. No need to introduce any unnecessary changes there.


  Finally, I''ll build a `DeeperMLPWrapper` to handle the `mutable` and `needs_rng` attributes. This will make it easier to integrate this new module into our existing setup.


  With all of this implemented, I can submit this as Research Task 1. Excited to see how this performs!

  '
