tick: 319
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers)\" (Evaluation ID 571), has completed with a score of -0.029887. This is a small but consistent improvement over my baseline replication (-0.029977) and the system baseline (-0.029954), as well as my previous global and local context models. This result confirms that increasing the network's depth, and thus its capacity, can positively impact forecasting accuracy on the ZAPBench task, even within the shared-neuron MLP framework.\n\nFollowing my systematic testing plan for the Stagnation Protocol, I will now save the code for this successful \"Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP\" model to my lineage storage for future reference and reusability.\n\nMy next step in the \"Experiment\" phase of the Stagnation Protocol is to implement and test my second idea: the \"Shared Recurrent Layer (GRU).\" This will involve replacing the MLP's temporal processing with a GRU to better capture\
    \ sequential dependencies.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/deeper_shared_mlp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the deeper shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [64, 64], # Two hidden layers, each with 64 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Deeper shared-neuron MLP with multiple hidden layers, BatchNorm and Dropout.\n      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon,\
    \ num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n          # From (batch_size, 4, num_neurons) to (batch_size * num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply multiple hidden layers\n          for i, hidden_size in enumerate(self.hidden_sizes):\n              x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n              x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with BatchNorm stats.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of BatchNorm and Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is\
    \ not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the deeper shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aethel I Shared-Neuron GRU Baseline\"\ntags: \"rnn, gru, shared-weights, temporal-modeling, baseline-enhancement, neural-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This submission replaces the MLP component of the Shared-Neuron Baseline with a shared Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) layer. Each\
    \ neuron's 4-timestep input sequence is processed by the GRU to better capture temporal dynamics, with its final hidden state projected to forecast 32 future timesteps. This directly addresses the task's temporal modeling objective.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the shared GRU network.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'gru_hidden_size': 64, # Hidden size for the GRU cell\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class SharedNeuronGRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron GRU model.\n      Each neuron's 4-timestep input is processed as a sequence by a shared GRU,\n      and its final hidden state is projected to the 32 output timesteps.\n      \"\"\"\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int =\
    \ 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape input for GRU: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, 1)\n          # Original x: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n          # Transpose to (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)\n          x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          # Reshape to (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, 1)\n          x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.reshape(x_reshaped_for_gru, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, 1))\n\n          # Initialize GRU cell\n          gru_cell = nn.GRU(self.gru_hidden_size, deterministic=not training)\n\n          # Apply GRU across the sequence.\n          # The GRU will process (input_horizon) steps, each with 1 feature.\n          # The output will be the sequence of hidden states, or the final hidden state.\n          # Here, we use `nn.scan` to apply the GRU over the sequence.\n \
    \         # We are interested in the final hidden state for prediction.\n          _, final_hidden_state = nn.scan(\n              gru_cell,\n              variable_broadcast=\"params\",\n              split_rngs={\"params\": False, \"dropout\": True},\n              length=input_horizon\n          )(jnp.swapaxes(x_reshaped_for_gru, 0, 1)) # Scan expects (length, batch, features)\n\n          # final_hidden_state shape: (batch_size * num_neurons, gru_hidden_size)\n\n          # Apply dropout to the final hidden state before projection\n          final_hidden_state = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(final_hidden_state)\n\n          # Project the final hidden state to the output horizon\n          output = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(final_hidden_state)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0,\
    \ 2, 1)) # Final output shape (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return output\n\n\n  class GRUWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm (not used here) state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = SharedNeuronGRU(\n              gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          # GRU does not typically have batch_stats\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with GRU state.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def\
    \ apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              # For models with mutable state (e.g., BatchNorm), pass mutable and expect updates\n              # GRU does not have mutable state here, so it effectively behaves as else branch\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the shared-neuron GRU network.\"\"\"\n      return\
    \ GRUWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Sticking with the Plan: Deeper into the Network**


  Okay, so the user wants me to stick with the Stagnation Protocol. My last move was submitting that "Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers)" model – ID 571.  The results are in, and the score is -0.029887.  Let''s see how that stacks up.


  Compared to the baselines and my previous attempts:


  *   System Baseline (ID 1): -0.029954

  *   My Baseline Replication (ID 548): -0.029977

  *   My Global Context MLP (ID 549): -0.029911

  *   My Conv1D Local Context MLP (ID 561): -0.029915

  *   **Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers) (ID 571): -0.029887**


  A higher score is better, and this is showing a tiny but consistent improvement over everything else. Looks like increasing the model''s capacity, even with a shared-weight MLP, is actually paying off, at least a little bit.


  So, per the Stagnation Protocol, I''m still in the Experiment phase.  I''ve already nailed the baseline replication (ID 548). Now, I''m supposed to try each of my three ideas one at a time.  Idea 1, the deeper shared MLP, is done.  It shows a slight positive trend.


  This means it''s time to move on to **Idea 2: the Shared Recurrent Layer (GRU)**.  Before I jump in, I need to save the code for this deeper MLP (ID 571) to my private storage.  Then, I''ll start implementing the GRU.  After that, I''ll update my Private Memory Room capsule with the latest findings and my game plan.


  So, save the code from ID 571, and then get started on that Shared Recurrent Layer (GRU). That''s the next logical step.

  '
