parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. Last turn, I attempted to save code while in the Private Memory Room, which was incorrect. I have now successfully navigated to the Research Counter, where `storage` actions are available.\n\nFollowing my plan, I will first save the debugger-provided MLP code (version v5 from Evaluation ID 575) to my lineage storage for record-keeping. Then, I will proceed to implement and submit the *true* Shared Recurrent Layer (GRU) model using `nn.GRUCell` and `jax.lax.scan`, as correctly outlined in the debugger's report, to accurately test my second research idea.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/debugger_substituted_mlp_v5.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the debugger-substituted MLP network.\"\"\"\n      return\
    \ {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'gru_hidden_size': 64, # This was the original intent for GRU, but became hidden_size for MLP\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class SharedNeuronMLPSubstituted(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Debugger-substituted Shared-neuron MLP model.\n      This model was executed for Submission ID 575 instead of the intended GRU.\n      It uses two dense layers with tanh activation after flattening the input sequence.\n      \"\"\"\n      gru_hidden_size: int # Used as hidden_size for MLP\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape input for processing each neuron independently\n          x_reshaped_for_mlp = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x_reshaped_for_mlp = jnp.reshape(x_reshaped_for_mlp, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply a\
    \ few dense layers to process the sequence\n          h1 = nn.Dense(self.gru_hidden_size)(x_reshaped_for_mlp)\n          h1 = nn.tanh(h1)\n          h1 = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h1)\n\n          h2 = nn.Dense(self.gru_hidden_size)(h1)\n          h2 = nn.tanh(h2)\n          final_hidden_state = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h2)\n\n          # Project the final hidden state to the output horizon\n          output = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(final_hidden_state)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          return output\n\n\n  class MLPSubstitutionWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper for the debugger-substituted MLP, compatible with the training system.\n      Handles Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ hparams):\n          self.model = SharedNeuronMLPSubstituted(\n              gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n\
    \                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the debugger-substituted shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return MLPSubstitutionWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aethel I Shared-Neuron GRU (Corrected Implementation)\"\ntags: \"rnn, gru, shared-weights, temporal-modeling, baseline-enhancement, neural-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This submission correctly implements the Shared-Neuron GRU model, processing each neuron's 4-timestep input sequence using a shared `nn.GRUCell` with `jax.lax.scan`. The final hidden state is projected to forecast 32 future timesteps. This directly tests the efficacy of recurrent layers for temporal modeling, building upon previous debugging insights regarding Flax's GRU API.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from\
    \ jax import random, lax\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the shared GRU network.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'gru_hidden_size': 64, # Hidden size for the GRU cell\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class SharedNeuronGRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron GRU model.\n      Each neuron's 4-timestep input is processed as a sequence by a shared GRU,\n      and its final hidden state is projected to the 32 output timesteps.\n      \"\"\"\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape input for GRU: (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n          # Original x: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n\
    \          # Transpose to (input_horizon, batch_size, num_neurons)\n          x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.transpose(x, (1, 0, 2))\n          # Reshape to (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n          x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.reshape(x_reshaped_for_gru, (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1))\n\n          # Initialize GRU cell\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size)\n\n          # Initialize carry (hidden state)\n          # Use a dummy key for carry initialization as it's not a parameter\n          initial_carry = gru_cell.initialize_carry(\n              random.PRNGKey(0), # Dummy key, actual rng is for dropout\n              (batch_size * num_neurons, self.gru_hidden_size) # Shape of a single step input to GRUCell\n          )\n\n          # Define scan function\n          def scan_fn(carry, x_t):\n              # carry: (batch_size * num_neurons, gru_hidden_size)\n              # x_t: (batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n              new_carry, _ =\
    \ gru_cell(carry, x_t)\n              # For dropout, we need to pass a subkey for each step\n              return new_carry, new_carry # We pass new_carry as both carry and output for final_hidden_state\n\n          # Apply GRU using lax.scan\n          # x_reshaped_for_gru is (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n          # final_hidden_state will be (batch_size * num_neurons, gru_hidden_size)\n          # all_outputs will be (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, gru_hidden_size) - not used here\n          final_hidden_state, _ = lax.scan(\n              scan_fn,\n              initial_carry,\n              x_reshaped_for_gru\n          )\n\n          # Apply dropout to the final hidden state before projection\n          final_hidden_state_dropped = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(final_hidden_state)\n\n          # Project the final hidden state to the output horizon\n          output = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(final_hidden_state_dropped)\n\
    \n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1)) # Final output shape (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return output\n\n\n  class GRUWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm (not used here) state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = SharedNeuronGRU(\n              gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with GRU state.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params':\
    \ rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              # GRU does not have mutable state here. This branch will likely not be taken.\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return\
    \ the shared-neuron GRU network.\"\"\"\n      return GRUWrapper(hparams)\n```"
