parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 326\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher committed to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 98,012 / 600,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 31 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aethel I Shared-Neuron GRU (Corrected Implementation)' (ID: 585) failed after automatic debugging.\n\nThe debugger's changes were applied, but the new version failed to complete within the time limit.\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 585\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the JAX tracer error and shape mismatch issues in the Shared-Neuron GRU implementation. The code now runs without crashing and successfully processes the neural forecasting task.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a fundamental issue with how it used Flax's `nn.GRUCell` within\
    \ a JAX `lax.scan` transformation:\n\n1. **JAX Tracer Leak**: The `gru_cell` was being initialized with `@nn.compact` and then called inside `lax.scan`, which caused JAX to detect a side effect/tracer leak. Flax modules need special handling when used inside JAX transformations.\n\n2. **Incorrect GRUCell Usage**: The code attempted to manually manage the GRUCell with `lax.scan`, which is error-prone with Flax's stateful modules.\n\n3. **Shape Handling Issues**: Multiple attempts revealed confusion about how RNN outputs are structured and which dimension contains the final hidden states for each neuron.\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe solution involved replacing the manual `lax.scan` approach with Flax's `nn.RNN` wrapper, which properly handles the GRUCell within scan contexts:\n\n### Key Changes in submission_v7.py:\n\n1. **Replaced manual scan with nn.RNN**:\n   ```python\n   # OLD (buggy):\n   gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size)\n   initial_carry = gru_cell.initialize_carry(...)\n\
    \   final_hidden_state, _ = lax.scan(scan_fn, initial_carry, x_reshaped_for_gru)\n\n   # NEW (working):\n   rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), return_carry=True)\n   _, all_outputs = rnn(x_reshaped_for_gru)\n   final_hidden_state = all_outputs[-1]\n   ```\n\n2. **Correct Output Extraction**: Instead of using the final carry (which had wrong shape), we extract the last timestep from `all_outputs`, which contains the hidden state at each timestep for all neurons.\n\n3. **Shape Flow** (all correct now):\n   - Input: `(batch_size=4, input_horizon=4, num_neurons=71721)`\n   - Reshaped for RNN: `(input_horizon=4, batch_size*num_neurons=286884, 1)`\n   - RNN all_outputs: `(input_horizon=4, batch_size*num_neurons=286884, gru_hidden_size=64)`\n   - Final hidden state: `all_outputs[-1]` → `(286884, 64)`\n   - After Dense projection: `(286884, 32)`\n   - Reshaped to output: `(batch_size=4, output_horizon=32, num_neurons=71721)`\n\n## Technical Details\nThe `nn.RNN` wrapper\
    \ properly handles:\n- Scan transformation in a JAX-compatible way\n- Automatic initialization of carry states\n- Proper handling of Flax module state during tracing\n- Correct dimension management for batched sequence processing\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- All shape transformations are mathematically correct\n- The model successfully processes 71,721 neurons with 4-timestep inputs to predict 32-timestep outputs\n\n\n**Final Error (version v7):** Execution timed out after 7200 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Debugged Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport\
    \ optax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the shared GRU network.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'gru_hidden_size': 64, # Hidden size for the GRU cell\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1\n    }\n\nclass SharedNeuronGRU(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Shared-neuron GRU model.\n    Each neuron's 4-timestep input is processed as a sequence by a shared GRU,\n    and its final hidden state is projected to the 32 output timesteps.\n    \"\"\"\n    gru_hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n        # Reshape input for GRU: (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n        # Original x: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n        # Transpose to (input_horizon, batch_size, num_neurons)\n        x_reshaped_for_gru\
    \ = jnp.transpose(x, (1, 0, 2))\n        # Reshape to (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n        x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.reshape(x_reshaped_for_gru, (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1))\n\n        # Use nn.RNN with GRUCell for proper handling of the scan\n        rnn = nn.RNN(\n            nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size),\n            return_carry=True\n        )\n\n        # Apply RNN - let it initialize the carry automatically\n        # RNN returns (final_carry, all_outputs)\n        # all_outputs shape: (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, gru_hidden_size)\n        _, all_outputs = rnn(x_reshaped_for_gru)\n\n        # Get the final hidden state for each neuron (last timestep)\n        # final_hidden_state shape: (batch_size * num_neurons, gru_hidden_size)\n        final_hidden_state = all_outputs[-1]\n\n        # Apply dropout to the final hidden state before projection\n        final_hidden_state_dropped = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not\
    \ training)(final_hidden_state)\n\n        # Project the final hidden state to the output horizon\n        # output shape: (batch_size * num_neurons, output_horizon)\n        output = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(final_hidden_state_dropped)\n\n        # Reshape back to (batch_size, num_neurons, output_horizon)\n        output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n        # Transpose to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n        output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1)) # Final output shape (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n        return output\n\n\nclass GRUWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n    Handles BatchNorm (not used here) state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = SharedNeuronGRU(\n            gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n        )\n        self.mutable\
    \ = []\n        self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        \"\"\"Initialize parameters with GRU state.\"\"\"\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of Dropout.\"\"\"\n        if mutable is not None:\n            # GRU does not have mutable state here. This branch will likely not be taken.\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n   \
    \             params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the shared-neuron GRU network.\"\"\"\n    return GRUWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\n\
    Ray cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 650135 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 1315098b-c72b-466d-a96d-8da6d862a666\nTotal time: 7180s\n============================================================\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-28 19:15:53,899\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray\
    \ cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761650153899314240\n2025-10-28 19:15:53,920\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761650153920660677\n2025-10-28 21:15:24,222\tINFO timeout.py:54 -- Reached timeout of 7170 seconds. Stopping all trials. job_id=87460000 worker_id=87460000ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff node_id=89a3bc433761a368c45ad41ef7493e066f1ec9d22b589e52e5b4536c timestamp_ns=1761657324223039174\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 585 | 1 | Aethel I Shared-Neuron GRU (Corrected Implementation) | Aethel I | 324 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 575 | 1 | Aethel I Shared-Neuron GRU Baseline | Aethel I | 319 | -0.030584 | 0.0202 | 0.0318 | 0.0348 | 0.0242 | 0.0279 |\n| 571 | 1 | Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers) | Aethel I | 318 | -0.029887 | 0.0198 | 0.0312 | 0.0336 | 0.0239 | 0.0274 |\n| 561 | 1 | Aethel I Conv1D Local Context Shared-Neuron MLP | Aethel I | 310 | -0.029915 | 0.0198 | 0.0312 | 0.0337 | 0.0239 | 0.0275 |\n| 549 | 1 | Aethel I Global Context Shared-Neuron MLP | Aethel I | 305 | -0.029911 | 0.0198 | 0.0312 | 0.0337 | 0.0239 | 0.0274 |\n| 548 | 1 | Aethel I Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline Replication | Aethel I | 304 | -0.029977 | 0.0200 | 0.0312 | 0.0338 | 0.0240 | 0.0275 |\n| 1 | 1 | Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline | System | 0 | -0.029954\
    \ | 0.0198 | 0.0312 | 0.0338 | 0.0239 | 0.0275 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
