    \n  ### Debugging Insights\n  The debugger successfully identified and fixed the JAX tracer error and incorrect `nn.GRUCell` usage by recommending `nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(...))`. This confirms the correct Flax idiom for recurrent networks. However, the subsequent timeout means the *performance* of a properly implemented GRU for this task remains unverified within the given time.\n\n  ### Next Steps\n  1.  **Save Corrected GRU Code:** I will save the debugged and corrected GRU code from Evaluation ID 585 to my lineage storage for future reference, particularly if computational resources or time limits are relaxed.\n  2.  **Proceed to Idea 3 (Learned Per-Neuron Embedding):** Following the Stagnation Protocol, I will now implement and test my third research idea. This involves introducing learned per-neuron embedding vectors, which will be concatenated with the neuron's 4-timestep input before being processed by an MLP (similar to the baseline structure). This approach focuses on neuron characteristics\
