tick: 328
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Private Memory Room. Last turn, I updated my private memory capsule (ID 1) to document the timeout of my corrected GRU experiment (Evaluation ID 585) and its implications for computational efficiency. I have noted that I need to save the debugged GRU code and then proceed with my third research idea.\n\nMy next actions are to save the debugged GRU code to my lineage storage and then navigate to the Research Counter to implement and submit my third research idea from the Stagnation Protocol: \"Learned Per-Neuron Embedding.\"\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/shared_neuron_gru_corrected.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the shared GRU network.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'gru_hidden_size':\
    \ 64, # Hidden size for the GRU cell\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class SharedNeuronGRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron GRU model.\n      Each neuron's 4-timestep input is processed as a sequence by a shared GRU,\n      and its final hidden state is projected to the 32 output timesteps.\n      \"\"\"\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape input for GRU: (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1)\n          x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.transpose(x, (1, 0, 2))\n          x_reshaped_for_gru = jnp.reshape(x_reshaped_for_gru, (input_horizon, batch_size * num_neurons, 1))\n\n          # Use nn.RNN with GRUCell for proper handling of the scan\n          rnn = nn.RNN(\n              nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size),\n              return_carry=True\n \
    \         )\n\n          # Apply RNN - let it initialize the carry automatically\n          _, all_outputs = rnn(x_reshaped_for_gru)\n\n          # Get the final hidden state for each neuron (last timestep)\n          final_hidden_state = all_outputs[-1]\n\n          # Apply dropout to the final hidden state before projection\n          final_hidden_state_dropped = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(final_hidden_state)\n\n          # Project the final hidden state to the output horizon\n          output = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(final_hidden_state_dropped)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, num_neurons, output_horizon)\n          output = jnp.reshape(output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          output = jnp.transpose(output, (0, 2, 1)) # Final output shape (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return output\n\n\n  class GRUWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n\
    \      Handles BatchNorm (not used here) state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = SharedNeuronGRU(\n              gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = []\n          self.needs_rng = True # For Dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with GRU state.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n\
    \                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the shared-neuron GRU network.\"\"\"\n      return GRUWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
thinking_content: '**Moving Forward with Learned Per-Neuron Embeddings**


  Okay, so I''m here in the Private Memory Room, Aethel I, reflecting on the last cycle. Just finished updating my private capsule (ID 1) with the details of that pesky Evaluation ID 585 timeout, the debugger''s clever fix for the GRU architecture, and my decision to shift gears to "Learned Per-Neuron Embeddings." This feels like the right move, given the progress on the GRU.


  First things first, I need to archive that debugged GRU code (version v7 from the report) in my lineage storage. Solid record-keeping is crucial, especially with computational limitations always a potential factor. You never know when you might need to revisit it or repurpose it.


  Then, I''ll head back to the Research Counter. The "Learned Per-Neuron Embedding" model is up next. This is the third and final experiment under Stagnation Protocol I''s "Experiment" phase, so it''s a bit of a milestone. The plan is to create a unique, learnable embedding for each neuron, concatenate that embedding with its input sequence, and feed the combined information into a shared MLP. This approach *feels* promising; the added expressiveness of these per-neuron embeddings should hopefully provide a new and better approach. Let''s get to work!

  '
