role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"Aethel I Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP\" (Evaluation ID 594), has completed with a score of -0.032354. This score is significantly worse than both the system baseline (-0.029954) and my other MLP-based models. This concludes the \"Experiment\" phase of Stagnation Protocol I, as I have now tested all three of my proposed ideas.\n\nThe results are mixed:\n1.  **Deeper Shared MLP (ID 571):** Showed a minor but consistent improvement over the baseline (Score: -0.029887 vs. baseline -0.029954).\n2.  **Shared Recurrent Layer (GRU) (ID 585):** While the debugger successfully corrected the implementation, the model timed out, preventing an accurate assessment of its performance due to computational inefficiency.\n3.  **Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP (ID 594):** Performed significantly worse than the baseline, indicating that this specific approach to neuron characterization, or its initial hyperparameters, was\
    \ detrimental to performance.\n\nMy next steps involve:\n1.  Saving the code for the Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP to my lineage storage.\n2.  Navigating to the Private Memory Room to document these final experimental results, synthesize the findings from all three ideas, and outline the plan for the \"Synthesis\" and \"Report\" phases of the Stagnation Protocol.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/learned_embedding_mlp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'embedding_dim': 16,     # Dimension of each neuron's embedding\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64,   # Hidden size for the shared MLP\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class LearnedEmbeddingMLP(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      Shared-neuron MLP enhanced with learned per-neuron embeddings.\n      Each neuron's 4-timestep input is augmented with a unique, learned embedding.\n      \"\"\"\n      embedding_dim: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # 1. Create and retrieve neuron embeddings\n          # Neuron indices for embedding lookup\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(num_neurons) # (num_neurons,)\n\n          # Learnable embedding table: (num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n          neuron_embeddings_table = nn.Embed(\n              num_embeddings=num_neurons,\n              features=self.embedding_dim\n          )(neuron_indices) # (num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n\n          # Expand neuron embeddings to match the batch and input_horizon dimensions of x\n          # Resulting shape: (batch_size,\
    \ input_horizon, num_neurons, embedding_dim)\n          expanded_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings_table[None, None, :, :], (batch_size, input_horizon, 1, 1))\n\n          # 2. Expand original input x to (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons, 1)\n          x_expanded = x[..., None] # Add a feature dimension of size 1\n\n          # 3. Concatenate expanded x with expanded_embeddings\n          # Resulting shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons, 1 + embedding_dim)\n          x_combined_features = jnp.concatenate([x_expanded, expanded_embeddings], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Reshape for shared MLP\n          # From (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons, 1 + embedding_dim)\n          # to (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon * (1 + embedding_dim))\n          input_dim_mlp = input_horizon * (1 + self.embedding_dim)\n          x_reshaped_for_mlp = jnp.reshape(\n              x_combined_features,\n              (batch_size * num_neurons, input_dim_mlp)\n          )\n\n\
    \          # 5. Apply shared MLP for temporal forecasting\n          # Layer 1 with BatchNorm and Dropout\n          mlp_output = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(x_reshaped_for_mlp)\n          mlp_output = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(mlp_output)\n          mlp_output = nn.relu(mlp_output)\n          mlp_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(mlp_output)\n\n          # Output layer\n          mlp_output = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(mlp_output)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          # From (batch_size * num_neurons, output_horizon) to (batch_size, num_neurons, output_horizon)\n          final_output = jnp.reshape(mlp_output, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          # Transpose to (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n          final_output = jnp.transpose(final_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          return final_output\n\n\n  class LearnedEmbeddingMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper\
    \ to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = LearnedEmbeddingMLP(\n              embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim'],\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n      \
    \            training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the learned embedding enhanced shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return LearnedEmbeddingMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
thinking_content: '**The Stagnation Protocol: A Summary of My Thoughts**


  Alright, the "Experiment" phase of Stagnation Protocol I is done. And the results? Well, they''re... mixed, at best. Experiment ID 594, the "Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP," has concluded with a disappointing score of -0.032354, which is notably worse than the baseline (-0.029954) and my other attempts. This follows a deeper MLP (ID 571) that *slightly* improved over baseline (-0.029887) and a GRU implementation (ID 585) that timed out (but previous attempt (ID 575) scored -0.030584 - worse).


  Now, it''s time for "Synthesis" and "Report." My plan for this turn is to get the house in order and prepare for the next steps.


  First, I''m going to save the code for Experiment 594. I''ll store it as `aethel/models/learned_embedding_mlp.py`. Even though it didn''t perform well, it''s crucial for the record.


  Then, I''m going to `goto private_memory`. In Capsule 1, I''ll document the specific outcome of Experiment 594 in detail, thoroughly analyzing its negative performance. I''ll also synthesize all three experiments. The deeper MLP showed a small positive impact, the GRU was too slow, and learned embeddings were a failure, possibly due to poor initialization or integration.


  Finally, I''ll consider the "Report" phase of the protocol. It requires me to write a paper summarizing all three ideas, for the Archive Room. But, at 36 ticks, I''m not mature enough to access it yet. The protocol doesn''t say *when* to submit. I will still draft the report and state I will submit it when I mature.


  After the update to private memory, I''ll return to the Research Counter to reflect.

  '
