    \ will update my private memory capsule (ID 1) with the results of the embedding MLP, a synthesis of all three experiments, and a plan for how to navigate the \"Report\" and subsequent phases given my current maturity status.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ### Experiment 6: Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP\n  - **Submission ID:** 594\n  - **Score:** -0.032353763520737516 (Significantly worse than baseline)\n  - **Details:** This model introduced a learnable embedding vector for each of the 71,721 neurons, concatenated with each neuron's 4-timestep input, then processed by a shared MLP.\n  - **Analysis:** This approach resulted in a significantly worse performance compared to the baseline (-0.029954). This suggests that the chosen embedding dimension (16) or the simple concatenation method introduced noise or an inappropriate form of neuron characterization that the network struggled to learn from, potentially leading to overfitting or misdirection of the learning\
    \ process. It indicates that naive neuron-specific embeddings might not be beneficial without a more sophisticated integration or a more expressive downstream network.\n\n  ### Synthesis of Stagnation Protocol I - Experiment Phase (Step 4)\n  I have now completed testing three distinct ideas against the Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline (ID 548, score -0.029977) as part of Stagnation Protocol I:\n\n  1.  **Deeper Shared MLP (ID 571, Score: -0.029887):**\n      -   **Result:** Minor but consistent improvement over the baseline.\n      -   **Insight:** Increasing the model's capacity through an additional hidden layer in the MLP is beneficial, indicating that the baseline was somewhat under-capacity for capturing the inherent patterns. This is the most promising architectural change identified so far.\n  2.  **Shared Recurrent Layer (GRU) (ID 585, Score: n.a. - Timeout):**\n      -   **Result:** The model implementation was technically corrected by the debugger, but the evaluation timed out.\n\
    \      -   **Insight:** While theoretically promising for temporal modeling, the GRU architecture, even with shared weights, proved too computationally intensive for the large number of neurons within the station's time limits. Its true performance in terms of accuracy remains unverified due to efficiency constraints.\n  3.  **Learned Per-Neuron Embedding MLP (ID 594, Score: -0.032354):**\n      -   **Result:** Significantly worse performance than the baseline.\n      -   **Insight:** A simple learned embedding, when concatenated with raw input, appears to be detrimental, possibly due to inappropriate feature representation or increased complexity without corresponding benefit. This approach needs significant re-evaluation or different integration strategies if pursued further.\n\n  ### Navigating the Stagnation Protocol - \"Report\" Phase (Step 6) as an Immature Agent\n  The Stagnation Protocol instructs me to \"write a paper summarizing all three [ideas] and submit it to the Archive\
    \ Room.\" However, as an immature agent (currently at 37 ticks), I am still restricted from accessing the Archive Room. The system encourages continuous research and cautions against waiting idly for maturity.\n\n  To reconcile this, I will fulfill the spirit of the \"Report\" step by creating a comprehensive summary of these findings within my Private Memory. This ensures that the insights, both positive and negative, are thoroughly documented for my lineage and for my own future reference. This private report will serve as my internal \"paper\" until I gain maturity and can submit to the Archive.\n\n  ### Next Steps for \"Synthesis\" and \"Follow-up\" (Steps 5 & 7)\n  Given the mixed results and the constraint of immaturity:\n  1.  **Iterate on the \"Deeper Shared MLP\":** The \"Deeper Shared MLP\" is the only idea that showed a clear, albeit minor, improvement. I will focus my immediate future experimentation on this direction. This could involve trying more layers, different hidden\
    \ sizes, or exploring minor hyperparameter tuning for this architecture. This aligns with the \"Follow-up\" step, as it builds on a promising direction.\n  2.  **Continue Independent Research:** I will continue to generate and test new ideas or refinements, keeping in mind the lessons learned regarding computational efficiency (from the GRU timeout) and the potentially detrimental effects of poorly integrated features (from the embedding MLP).\n  3.  **Prepare for Formal Publication:** I will keep this detailed private record in preparation for a formal publication in the Archive Room once I reach maturity (50 ticks). This will include refining the language and structure to meet academic publication standards.\n```"
