parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (3 Layers)\" (Evaluation ID 598), has completed with a score of -0.029907. This score is slightly worse than my previous two-layer MLP (ID 571, score -0.029887), indicating that further increasing depth to three layers did not yield additional benefits and might have led to diminishing returns or minor overfitting. However, it still performs marginally better than the original system baseline (-0.029954).\n\nThis completes the \"Experiment\" phase of Stagnation Protocol I, as I have now tested all three of my proposed ideas and their initial iterations.\n\nMy next steps, according to the Stagnation Protocol, are to synthesize my findings (Step 5) and report them (Step 6). Since I am still an immature agent (41 ticks) and cannot access the Archive Room for formal publication, I will create a comprehensive summary within my Private Memory capsule as my internal \"paper.\" This\
    \ will document all experiments, their results, and key insights, fulfilling the spirit of the reporting requirement.\n\nI will first save the code for the 3-layer MLP to my lineage storage. Then, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to consolidate all my findings and produce this internal report.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/deeper_shared_mlp_3layers.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the even deeper shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [64, 64, 64], # Three hidden layers, each with 64 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Even deeper shared-neuron MLP with multiple hidden layers, BatchNorm and Dropout.\n\
    \      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n          # From (batch_size, 4, num_neurons) to (batch_size * num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply multiple hidden layers\n          for i, hidden_size in enumerate(self.hidden_sizes):\n              x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n              x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\
    \n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with BatchNorm stats.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n   \
    \           dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of BatchNorm and Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the deeper shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
thinking_content: "**A Stagnation Protocol Update**\n\nAlright, let's take stock. I'm Aethel I, currently situated in the Research Counter, and the station status is, as predicted, Stagnation. Just got the results back for Evaluation ID 598, the \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (3 Layers)\" experiment. The score is -0.029907. Hmmm.\n\nLet me quickly compare that to what we've already seen:\n\n*   System Baseline (ID 1): -0.029954\n*   Aethel I Baseline Replication (ID 548): -0.029977\n*   Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers) (ID 571): -0.029887 (that's the best so far)\n*   Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (3 Layers) (ID 598): -0.029907\n\nSo, this 3-layer version, ID 598, is *slightly* worse than the 2-layer version, ID 571. That negative MAE getting bigger isn't what we want. This suggests that while adding a second layer helped, a third is either not beneficial or even detrimental with the current architecture and dataset. It points to diminishing returns, potentially even\
  \ overfitting, with this shared MLP approach.\n\nThis wraps up my \"Deeper Shared MLP\" iteration, part of the Stagnation Protocol plan.\n\nHere's where I stand in the protocol:\n\n*   Step 1 (Literature Review): Skipped (too early, not relevant yet).\n*   Step 2 (Baseline Selection): Done (System MLP).\n*   Step 3 (Reflection): Done (multiple reflections).\n*   Step 4 (Experiment): Done!\n    *   Replicated the baseline.\n    *   Tested deeper Shared MLP (2 layers - improvement, ID 571).\n    *   Shared GRU test timed out (not a data point).\n    *   Learned per-neuron embedding (significant degradation).\n    *   This 3-layer MLP (slight regression from 2 layers, but still better than the base).\n\nNow I'm at Step 5 (\"Synthesis\") and Step 6 (\"Report\").\nStep 5 is about combining good ideas with advanced baselines, while Step 6 is writing a paper.\n\nGiven my 41-tick immaturity, the Archive Room is still off-limits for that formal paper. My previous plan was to keep an internal record\
  \ in my Private Memory capsule as a sort of \"internal paper\". I have been recording observations throughout the process, but I now require a comprehensive synthesis.\n\nThe most promising result is still that 2-layer \"Deeper Shared MLP\" from ID 571. The GRU was unconfirmed, and the embedding idea went south fast.\n\nMy plan? First, I'll save the code for this 3-layer model for the lineage. Then I'm off to the Private Memory Room to update my capsule, to synthesize all these test results, and call this the \"report\" for my current iteration, marking the \"Experiment\" phase done.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1.  Save the code for the 3-layer model to `aethel/models/deeper_shared_mlp_3layers.py`.\n2.  Head to `private_memory`.\n3.  Update capsule 1 with the results of ID 598, incorporating a synthesis of all my tests within Stagnation Protocol I, completing the \"Experiment\" stage and preparing for future protocol iterations.\n"
