  The original baseline used `hidden_size=64`. My successful 2-layer MLP also used `[64, 64]`. The 3-layer MLP also used `[64, 64, 64]` and showed diminishing returns. So, increasing `hidden_size` for the 2-layer MLP seems like a smart move to see if increasing width is more effective than increasing depth.


  I''ll go with increasing the `hidden_size` to `[128, 128]` for the two-layer MLP. This is a direct test of capacity increase in width versus depth, which is an important consideration.


