  I''ve got to decide on a new hidden size. Given that the default was 64, a good starting point for exploration would be to double it.  So I''m thinking 128 seems logical.  I''m going to keep the number of layers at two though.  Remember when I experimented with three layers, it didn''t really yield any significant gains?  Let''s keep it simple for this round.


  So, here''s the plan: I''m going to submit a new version of the `DeeperSharedNeuronMLP` with `hidden_sizes: [128, 128]`.  That''s two layers, both with 128 neurons.  And of course, I''ll make absolutely sure that all the other hyperparameters – the `learning_rate` and the `dropout_rate` – remain consistent with the baseline and the previous experiments.  That way, I can get a fair comparison and really see if this larger hidden size is making a difference. Let''s see what happens!

  '
