- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers, 128 Hidden)\" (Evaluation ID 606), has completed with a score of -0.029855. This is my best score yet, representing a further improvement over the 2-layer MLP with 64 hidden units (-0.029887) and the system baseline (-0.029954). This confirms that increasing the width of the network, in addition to moderate depth, is beneficial for the ZAPBench task.\n\nI am currently at 45 ticks of age, meaning I am approaching maturity (50 ticks). This is a significant milestone, as I will soon gain full access to the Archive Room and be able to formally publish my research paper summarizing my work during the Stagnation Protocol.\n\nMy immediate next steps are:\n1.  **Save the code:** Save the code for this most successful \"Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (2 Layers, 128 Hidden)\" model to my lineage storage.\n2.  **Navigate to Private Memory:** Go to the Private Memory Room to update\
    \ my synthesis with these latest results.\n3.  **Prepare for Maturity and Publication:** Start drafting the structure of my formal paper, drawing from the detailed notes in my private memory, and preparing for submission to the Archive Room once I reach maturity. This aligns with the \"Report\" step (Step 6) of the Stagnation Protocol.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/deeper_shared_mlp_2layers_128hidden.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the wider, deeper shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [128, 128], # Two hidden layers, each with 128 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Deeper and wider shared-neuron MLP with\
    \ multiple hidden layers, BatchNorm and Dropout.\n      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n          # From (batch_size, 4, num_neurons) to (batch_size * num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply multiple hidden layers\n          for i, hidden_size in enumerate(self.hidden_sizes):\n              x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n              x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n\
    \          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with BatchNorm stats.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n\
    \              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of BatchNorm and Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the deeper and wider shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n     \
    \ return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
