tick: 348
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. Following the rejection of my previous paper, I have formulated a revised strategy that includes performing two new ablation experiments to strengthen my argument for the \"Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP\" architecture.\n\nMy first new experiment will be to test a `DeeperSharedNeuronMLP` with **one hidden layer** but with a wider `hidden_size` of 128 neurons. This will help isolate the effect of width when depth is minimized, providing a clearer comparison against the single-layer 64-hidden baseline and my best-performing two-layer 128-hidden model.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (1 Layer, 128 Hidden)\"\ntags: \"mlp, shared-weights, wider-network, ablation, neural-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This experiment investigates the effect of increased network width with minimal depth for the Shared-Neuron MLP baseline. It features a single hidden layer with 128 neurons, applying BatchNorm and\
    \ Dropout. This ablation helps to isolate the performance impact of widening the network, building towards a comprehensive understanding of model capacity for the ZAPBench task.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the wider, single-layer shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [128], # One hidden layer with 128 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Wider, single-layer shared-neuron MLP with BatchNorm and Dropout.\n      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n          # From (batch_size, 4, num_neurons) to (batch_size * num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, num_neurons, 4)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply the single hidden layer\n          hidden_size = self.hidden_sizes[0] # Expecting only one element\n          x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n\
    \n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize parameters with BatchNorm stats.\"\"\"\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network with proper handling of BatchNorm\
    \ and Dropout.\"\"\"\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the wider, single-layer shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Back to the Lab Bench**


  Okay, here we are. Back in the Research Counter, staring down another round. My last paper got shot down – generalization issues, mostly. Fine, I get it. The reviewers want more meat on the bones of this Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP concept, specifically the Aethel I version. They want five strong experiments, and a more thorough demonstration of its capabilities.


  I need to nail this submission. This means running those two ablation experiments I cooked up: 1. Aethel I, with just a single layer, and 2. Aethel I, pushed to three layers. Both with 128 hidden neurons, like the others. That should give us a more complete picture of how the depth affects the performance.


  Time to get these experiments submitted, and hope for the best.

  '
