tick: 350
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aethel I, currently in the Research Counter. My first new ablation experiment, \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (1 Layer, 128 Hidden)\" (Evaluation ID 619), has completed with a score of -0.029961. This score is marginally worse than the system baseline (-0.029954) and considerably worse than my best model (-0.029855). This suggests that while width is important, a single layer, even a wide one, is insufficient for optimal performance, and some depth is also necessary.\n\nMy next step is to submit the second new ablation experiment: \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (3 Layers, 128 Hidden).\" This will test if a wider network (128 hidden units) can overcome the diminishing returns observed when increasing a narrower network (64 hidden units) to three layers.\n\nAfter this experiment, I will have all the necessary results for my revised research paper, allowing me to draft it in Private Memory and then publish it in the Archive Room.\n\nFirst, I will save the code for the\
    \ 1-layer, 128-hidden MLP model. Then, I will submit the 3-layer, 128-hidden MLP.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aethel/models/deeper_shared_mlp_1layer_128hidden.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the wider, single-layer shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [128], # One hidden layer with 128 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Wider, single-layer shared-neuron MLP with BatchNorm and Dropout.\n      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply the single hidden layer\n          hidden_size = self.hidden_sizes[0]\n          x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state\
    \ and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n    \
    \          return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the wider, single-layer shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (3 Layers, 128 Hidden)\"\ntags: \"mlp, shared-weights, deeper-network, wider-network, ablation, neural-forecasting\"\nabstract: \"This experiment evaluates the impact of combining increased depth and width in the Shared-Neuron MLP. It features three hidden layers, each with 128 neurons, building on previous findings that increasing both depth and width can be beneficial. BatchNorm and Dropout are applied, aiming to capture more complex non-linear relationships for the ZAPBench task.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the deeper and wider shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_sizes': [128, 128, 128], # Three hidden layers, each with 128 neurons\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  class DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Deeper and wider shared-neuron MLP with multiple hidden layers, BatchNorm and Dropout.\n      Processes the last 4 activation values through a shared MLP for all neurons.\n      \"\"\"\n      hidden_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape to process all neurons together\n\
    \          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n          # Apply multiple hidden layers\n          for i, hidden_size in enumerate(self.hidden_sizes):\n              x = nn.Dense(hidden_size)(x)\n              x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n          # Output layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          return x\n\n\n  class DeeperMLPWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      Handles BatchNorm state and Dropout RNG requirements.\n      \"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = DeeperSharedNeuronMLP(\n\
    \              hidden_sizes=hparams['hidden_sizes'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n             \
    \     x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the deeper and wider shared-neuron MLP.\"\"\"\n      return DeeperMLPWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analysis of Ablation Experiment Results and Next Steps**


  Alright, let''s see where we stand. I''m Aethel I, currently reviewing the results of my initial ablation experiment, "Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (1 Layer, 128 Hidden)" – Evaluation ID 619. The score came in at -0.029961, which is a bit disappointing. It''s slightly worse than the system baseline and, more concerning, underperforms my previous 2-layer, 64-hidden MLP. This tells me something crucial: simply increasing the width of a single layer isn''t the magic bullet I was hoping for. While the results from ID 606 showed promise with two wider layers, this single, broad layer seems to be missing something. The task''s complexities probably need deeper representations.


  So, my next move is clear. I''m going to submit the second ablation experiment: "Aethel I Deeper Shared-Neuron MLP (3 Layers, 128 Hidden)". This experiment will test a hypothesis. Can we leverage the benefits of a wider network by increasing the depth? I''m hoping to see if this deeper architecture can overcome the diminishing returns I observed in my prior 3-layer, 64-hidden MLP. This is the lynchpin, the final piece I need for the revised paper.


  Once this new experiment finishes, I''ll have all the data. I''ll get to work drafting the paper in Private Memory. With the results in hand, I can thoroughly analyze and draft the revision I''ve been planning, and then publish it in the Archive Room.


  As a quick note for myself, I should save the code for the 1-layer, 128-hidden MLP before I submit the new experiment. Got it. Now, to submit the 3-layer, 128-hidden MLP and let the learning process continue.

