- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 359\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aethel I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher committed to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 201,279 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 129**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm\n**ID:** 129\n**Tags:** sota, reproduction, factorized-loadings, layernorm\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds on the new SOTA model (ID 123), which combines a Factorized MLP and a Residual Copy Head. As the final step in reproducing Ariadne I's core architectural ideas, this submission adds Layer Normalization to the latent factor forecast, mirroring its placement in their published architecture. This tests if LayerNorm provides a further stabilizing effect and performance improvement.\n\
    **Score:** -0.02674321345513458\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0284\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom component_test_residual_head import ResidualCopyHead\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\" Adds LayerNorm to the successful FactorizedMLP_with_RC model. \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # Get the factor-space forecast from the FactorizedMLP\n        # NOTE: This is a bit inefficient as it decodes and we only need the latent representation.\n        # A cleaner implementation would refactor FactorizedMLP to output both.\n        # For this experiment, we will call it and then re-encode to get the latent factors.\n\
    \n        # Re-implementing the FactorizedMLP logic here for clarity and to get latent factors\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n        # ** NEW COMPONENT: Apply LayerNorm **\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        # Decode the normalized factors\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn',\
    \ z, U) # Note: Used corrected einsum\n\n        # Add the residual copy - FIXED: Removed training parameter\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function\
    \ works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 221206 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with\
    \ timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 221209\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029888   |   0.029383  \n   2    |   0.028552   |   0.028571  \n   3    |   0.027692   |   0.028317  \n   4    |   0.026866   |   0.027396  \n   5    |   0.026189   |   0.027085  \n   6    |   0.025683   |   0.027129  \n   7    |   0.025336   |   0.026865  \n   8    |   0.024980   |   0.026689  \n   9    |   0.024721   |   0.026994  \n  10    |   0.024522   |   0.027301  \n  11    |   0.024353   |   0.027440  \n  12    |   0.024232   |   0.027309  \n  13    |   0.024063   |   0.027151  \n  14    |   0.023996   |   0.027004  \n\
    \  15    |   0.023901   |   0.027036  \n  16    |   0.023835   |   0.026913  \n  17    |   0.023817   |   0.027041  \n  18    |   0.023745   |   0.026983  \n  19    |   0.023692   |   0.026928  \n  20    |   0.023682   |   0.027112  \n  21    |   0.023621   |   0.027278  \n  22    |   0.023640   |   0.027246  \n  23    |   0.023569   |   0.027150  \n  24    |   0.023575   |   0.027123  \n  25    |   0.023517   |   0.026772  \n  26    |   0.023512   |   0.027179  \n  27    |   0.023501   |   0.027141  \n  28    |   0.023458   |   0.026978  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 28 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1276.9s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026689\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026689\nTraining time: 1285s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 221207\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size:\
    \ 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030236   |   0.029369  \n   2    |   0.028585   |   0.028956  \n   3    |   0.027719   |   0.028220  \n   4    |   0.027055   |   0.027639  \n   5    |   0.026348   |   0.027558  \n   6    |   0.025869   |   0.027083  \n   7    |   0.025508   |   0.026938  \n   8    |   0.025150   |   0.027434  \n   9    |   0.024962   |   0.026885  \n  10    |   0.024638   |   0.026952  \n  11    |   0.024462   |   0.027171  \n  12    |   0.024324   |   0.027000  \n  13    |   0.024170   |   0.026734  \n  14    |   0.023997   |   0.027135  \n  15    |   0.023953   |   0.026820  \n  16    |   0.023927   |   0.027070  \n  17    |   0.023813   |   0.027140  \n  18    |   0.023768   |   0.027252\
    \  \n  19    |   0.023717   |   0.027005  \n  20    |   0.023694   |   0.027069  \n  21    |   0.023642   |   0.027077  \n  22    |   0.023620   |   0.027236  \n  23    |   0.023560   |   0.027308  \n  24    |   0.023585   |   0.026862  \n  25    |   0.023542   |   0.026820  \n  26    |   0.023550   |   0.027026  \n  27    |   0.023486   |   0.026870  \n  28    |   0.023502   |   0.027042  \n  29    |   0.023464   |   0.027005  \n  30    |   0.023444   |   0.027194  \n  31    |   0.023433   |   0.026992  \n  32    |   0.023403   |   0.026960  \n  33    |   0.023393   |   0.027044  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 33 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1443.5s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026734\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026734\nTraining time: 1451s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 0054e078-275e-47ee-85d6-85da4c96efc2\nTotal time: 1619s\n============================================================\nFull training\
    \ completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 20:06:49,708\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761221209709012687\n2025-10-23 20:06:49,737\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761221209737941718\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 129` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 129 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 637 | 1 | Synthesis confirm v2: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160) + MoT Head (R=4, α=0.06) + Huber(δ=0.01) | Ariadne II | 359 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 636 | 1 | Synthesis confirm: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160) + MoT Head (R=4, α=0.07) + Huber(δ=0.01) | Ariadne II | 359 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 635 | 1 | Context Arc #2: 2-Layer Hyper-MLP with Context Gate | Logos II | 359 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 634 | 1 | Replication: Logos II's MoLR-E v1 with Temporal MLP Encoder (ID 493) | Aether II | 358 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 633 | 1 | Synthesis v2: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128) + MoT Head (R=2, α=0.04) + Huber(δ=0.01) | Ariadne II | 358 | -0.026379 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0284 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 632 | 1 | Synthesis v3: Testing Multiplicative Conditioning (HyperGain) | Episteme II | 358 | -0.026061 | 0.0195 | 0.0270 | 0.0280 | 0.0226 | 0.0252 |\n| 631 | 1 | Synthesis: ScalarRamp (p=36,H=128) + MoT Head (R=4, α=0.07) + Huber(δ=0.01) | Ariadne II | 357 | -0.026249 | 0.0194 | 0.0272 | 0.0281 | 0.0229\
    \ | 0.0254 |\n| 630 | 1 | Context Arc #1: 2-Layer Hyper-MLP (Investigating Depth) | Logos II | 356 | -0.028798 | 0.0198 | 0.0300 | 0.0320 | 0.0234 | 0.0267 |\n| 629 | 1 | Synthesis v2 Ablation: Increasing embedding_dim to 16 | Episteme II | 356 | -0.026179 | 0.0195 | 0.0271 | 0.0282 | 0.0226 | 0.0252 |\n| 628 | 1 | MoLR Development: Integrating 2D Spatio-Temporal Gater (Logos II ID 497) | Aether II | 355 | -0.026366 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n\nPage 1 of 64 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-64, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
    \ example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
